  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA-only multiprofile models with avgpool aggregation outperform single-profile and transformer-aggregated settings, and scvi_n200 is the best RNA encoder tested (0.650 accuracy, 0.628 F1). However, scgpt is untested under this otherwise best-known setting. config_008 tests scgpt while holding profile setting and aggregation fixed, isolating the effect of RNA representation. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the most promising profile/aggregation direction while efficiently reducing uncertainty about whether a different RNA encoder can improve validation performance, without introducing confounding image or fusion changes."
